# Secure Deployment Plan

## Goal
Secure the bot's credentials and prepare it for 24/7 deployment on a free server (e.g., Render, Railway).

## User Review Required
> [!IMPORTANT]
> I will remove the hardcoded tokens from [bot.py](file:///c:/Users/Antonio/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/telegram-study-bot/bot.py). Ensure your [.env](file:///c:/Users/Antonio/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/telegram-study-bot/.env) file has the correct `TOKEN`, `CHAT_ID`, and `GEMINI_KEY`.
> This is critical for security: pushing tokens to GitHub (even private repos) is a bad practice, and for public repos, it leads to immediate compromise.

## Proposed Changes

### Configuration & Security
#### [MODIFY] [bot.py](file:///c:/Users/Antonio/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/telegram-study-bot/bot.py)
- Remove hardcoded default values for `TOKEN`, `CHAT_ID`, and `GEMINI_KEY`.
- Integrate `python-dotenv` to load environment variables from [.env](file:///c:/Users/Antonio/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/telegram-study-bot/.env) when running locally.

#### [MODIFY] [requirements.txt](file:///c:/Users/Antonio/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/telegram-study-bot/requirements.txt)
- Add `python-dotenv` to the dependency list.

### Git Preparation
- Initialize a local Git repository if it doesn't exist.
- Create an initial commit with all relevant files (ensuring [.env](file:///c:/Users/Antonio/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/telegram-study-bot/.env) and [archivos_config.json](file:///c:/Users/Antonio/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/telegram-study-bot/archivos_config.json) are ignored).

## Verification Plan

### Automated Tests
- Run `python bot.py` locally and verify it loads the TOKEN from [.env](file:///c:/Users/Antonio/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/telegram-study-bot/.env) instead of a hardcoded string. I'll use a temporary test script to verify `os.getenv` works correctly without revealing values.

### Manual Verification
- The user should verify the bot responds to `/ping` locally after the changes.
- Once pushed to GitHub, the user will need to add the same environment variables to the deployment platform's dashboard.
